WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Python does have inheritance and it also has multiple inheritance. I'm not going to jump into a lot of these topics

00:08.000 --> 00:15.000
but I do want to point out a few important things about inheritance. When one class inherits from another

00:15.000 --> 00:19.000
you will put the class that is being inherited from

00:19.000 --> 00:24.000
in parentheses after the definition of the class itself.

00:25.000 --> 00:30.000
When you are calling Dunder in it on that subclass,

00:30.000 --> 00:36.000
if you then want to run all of the code from the superclass,

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
you need to explicitly call super,

00:40.000 --> 00:45.000
and then the method that you would call in this case we know that we want to call Dunder in it,

00:45.000 --> 00:49.000
along with all of the arguments.

00:50.000 --> 00:56.000
This is syntax that you are very likely to run into, so it's important to keep track of.

00:56.000 --> 01:01.000
There is a lot more content here in the course about

01:01.000 --> 01:08.000
overriding variables and subclasses that I recommend you go back to and read later.

